# Pin the determinism of the parallelized createSectionContrib loop in
# PDBLinker::addSections (lld/COFF/PDB.cpp): the section contributions written
# to the PDB -- their order and per-chunk JamCRC -- must not depend on the
# number of link threads. Link the same inputs serially and in parallel, then
# require the dumped contributions to be byte-identical.
#
# Both links reuse the same /out and /pdb paths (the serial PDB is dumped before
# the parallel link overwrites it) and pin /pdbaltpath, so /threads: is the only
# difference. Otherwise the embedded PDB-path string would change the size of a
# synthesized .rdata chunk and make the contributions differ for reasons
# unrelated to the parallel loop.

# RUN: yaml2obj %p/Inputs/pdb1.yaml -o %t1.obj
# RUN: yaml2obj %p/Inputs/pdb2.yaml -o %t2.obj

# RUN: lld-link /debug /pdb:%t.pdb /pdbaltpath:test.pdb /dll /out:%t.dll \
# RUN:   /entry:main /nodefaultlib /threads:1 %t1.obj %t2.obj
# RUN: llvm-pdbutil dump -section-contribs %t.pdb > %t.serial.txt

# RUN: lld-link /debug /pdb:%t.pdb /pdbaltpath:test.pdb /dll /out:%t.dll \
# RUN:   /entry:main /nodefaultlib /threads:4 %t1.obj %t2.obj
# RUN: llvm-pdbutil dump -section-contribs %t.pdb > %t.parallel.txt

# Guard against both dumps being empty (which would make the diff vacuous).
# RUN: FileCheck --check-prefix=NONEMPTY --input-file=%t.serial.txt %s
# NONEMPTY: SC[

# RUN: diff -u %t.serial.txt %t.parallel.txt
